WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.900
Complete coverage index, part two.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:08.200
More one-line vocabulary, from chunking all the way to RLHF.

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.967
Four chunking terms to know.

4
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:13.567
Semantic chunking splits where meaning shifts.

5
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:20.233
Recursive chunking splits by structure, headings, then paragraphs, then sentences, until the size fits.

6
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:25.100
Overlapping chunks repeat some tokens between neighbours, so ideas aren't cut.

7
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.633
And context stuffing is the anti-pattern of cramming too many chunks in.

8
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:35.667
Document processing is the unglamorous work that sets your RAG quality ceiling.

9
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:40.437
PDF layout analysis detects columns, reading order, and tables.

10
00:00:40.437 --> 00:00:45.333
Table extraction pulls tables out as structured data, headers intact.

11
00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:51.467
And HTML, Markdown, and XML parsing strips boilerplate while preserving structure.

12
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:55.000
Retrieval has its own vocabulary.

13
00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:00.367
Dense retrieval uses embedding similarity, and sparse retrieval uses keywords.

14
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:05.444
Multi-stage retrieval does cheap wide recall, then precise reranking.

15
00:01:05.444 --> 00:01:11.467
Query decomposition breaks a compound question into sub-queries and retrieves for each.

16
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:15.033
Three approximate nearest neighbour index types.

17
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:20.567
IVFFlat partitions vectors into clusters and searches only the nearest few.

18
00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:25.400
IVF-PQ does the same, plus product quantization for compression.

19
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.567
And Redis Vector is vector search inside Redis, handy when it's already your cache.

20
00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:35.967
Answer correctness means matching ground truth, not merely being grounded.

21
00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:41.067
Recall at k and precision at k measure retrieval quality at a cutoff k.

22
00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:47.733
And ARES is an automated RAG evaluation framework, alongside RAGAS, DeepEval, and TruLens.

23
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:50.767
Agent patterns from the long tail.

24
00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:54.467
A router agent classifies a request, then dispatches it.

25
00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:58.400
A supervisor assigns work and reviews the workers' output.

26
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.944
Multi-agent setups can be hierarchical, peer-to-peer, collaborative, or competitive.

27
00:02:03.944 --> 00:02:06.567
That's who talks to whom, and who decides.

28
00:02:06.867 --> 00:02:12.400
And Gorilla is a model fine-tuned for accurate API calling, in the Toolformer lineage.

29
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.100
Here are the infrastructure terms around agents.

30
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.633
An autonomous agent runs multi-step without per-step human input.

31
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:24.167
The agent workflow is the defined sequence it follows.

32
00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:29.067
The runtime, or gateway, executes agents and brokers their tool traffic.

33
00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:33.567
And graph state is LangGraph's typed state object, passed between nodes.

34
00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:37.064
Full fine-tuning updates every weight.

35
00:02:37.064 --> 00:02:39.300
It's expensive, and risks forgetting.

36
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:47.915
Transfer learning reuses a pretrained model for a new task, and continual pre-training adds more pretraining on domain text.

37
00:02:47.915 --> 00:02:51.067
Domain adaptation is the goal behind all three.

38
00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:55.567
Layer-wise learning rate decay uses smaller rates for earlier layers.

39
00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:59.967
RLHF has four objects to keep straight.

40
00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:04.633
A preference dataset holds pairs of chosen and rejected responses.

41
00:03:04.933 --> 00:03:08.633
The reward model scores outputs by predicted human preference.

42
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:11.400
The policy model is the one being trained.

43
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.933
And the reference model is a frozen copy, which the KL penalty measures drift against.

44
00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:18.933
Let's recap.

45
00:03:18.933 --> 00:03:22.733
Chunking, parsing, and retrieval form the RAG vocabulary.

46
00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:26.733
ANN indexes and eval metrics tune and measure search.

47
00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:29.200
Agent patterns define who decides.

48
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.033
And fine-tuning and RLHF objects shape the model itself.
